  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Automation means using a machine to do a job, instead of a person."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "In the past, machines only did simple jobs."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "But nowadays they can do complicated work, too."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "This worries people."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "They fear they'll be made unemployed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "But is this true?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "It's complicated."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "Automation does replace certain jobs."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "But automation also creates jobs."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "In the past, bank workers feared ATMs would steal their jobs."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "But, in truth, more jobs were created."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "Banks employed more salespeople and accountants."
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "What do you think?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "What future jobs will be made by automation?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
